This is the simplified equivalent of what ggpairs does.

myt <- seq(0,1,0.01)*2*pi
mydf <- data.frame(
          myt = myt,
          x1 = sin(myt),
          x2 = sin(myt+0.05),
          x3 = sin(myt+pi/8),
          x4 =  cos(myt)

par(mfrow=c(4,4))
for (i in 1:4)
  for (j in 1:4)
    plot(mydf[,i],mydf[,j])

I would like to have

par(mfrow=c(4,4))
for (i in 1:4)
  for (j in 1:4)
    plot(mydf[,i],mydf[,j],type="l")

I think the data also illustrate why I would rather have lines than points.

