Perhaps scale_identity is really what you want (especially if you
really have more than 4 colour-culture pairs):

ggplot(df, aes(x = CULTURE, y = TAUX, fill=COULEUR)) +
    geom_bar(width = 0.9) +

    scale_fill_identity(name="LEGENDE")

No legend, but it is redundant in this example anyway.

Charlotte

