geom_hline is causing the line through the points. The legend is trying to integrate all of the elements. You could annotate the line instead of trying to integrate the legend.

ggplot(ddf, aes(x = x, y = y))+

geom_point(aes(colour="Observations", shape="Observations")) +
stat_summary(aes(colour = "Means", shape ="Means"),
                 fun.y = mean, fun.ymin = min, fun.ymax = max,
                 geom = "point") +

geom_hline(aes(yintercept = mean(y), linetype = "Overall Mean"), show_guide = F)+
annotate("text", x= "A", y= (mean(y)+0.1), label="Overall Mean")+
labs(x= "xAxisLable", y= "yAxisLabel", color="Observations", shape="Observations")

If you want the line to be a separate element in a joined legend... I don't think you can do that. Winston, Takahashi-san, or Hadley would be able to answer that absolutely. If you knew enough of the guts perhaps you could build what you want from scratch with grobs but that would be painful methinks.

