Munish,

The reduced example you posted is still pretty confusing, honestly.
But it looks like you want to make a plot using the input_df
dataframe, coloring the points (or whatever) according to the sd_input
dataframe's "sd" field. Is this right? If so, I would create a new
column in input_df like this:

input_df$pointcolor <- apply( input_df, 1, function(x){ which(
x["lat"] == sd_input$lat ) } )

This gives you a column in input_df, looked up from the values in
sd_input, that you can use in ggplot (e.g. color=pointcolor).

If this isn't what you want, please try to provide a simple,
super-short reproducible example!

Regards,
Ben

