On 2012-Jul-12, at 17:11 , Navi wrote:
>
> I am trying to plot some maps with multiple variables with different range of values. I do understand the scale issue with discrete and continuous variables, but am unable to implement it in the code to rescale my lengends.
> I am attaching the map output and the code that i used to generate it.
> I would like to be able to manipulate the scales here for each map and the package automatically generates a scale.
> Is there a way i can get the same maps (same colour combinations and boundaries) but with being able to redesign the scales and remove the "white" from the legend.

I'm not sure what you mean by "redesigning the scale". Look at scale_fill_gradient, scale_fill_gradient2  and scale_fill_gradientn.

For the white, that's easy: you want to *set* the boundary colour to be white, you don't want to *map* the aesthetic property to some variable, so it needs to be *outside* aes(). With this you won't need the scale_colour_manual call.

